---
layout: layouts/simulation.njk
title: "The Great Exchange"
subtitle: "Interactive Economic History Lab"
description: "Teaching Money Emergence Through the Kiyotaki-Wright Model"
pageClass: "lab-homepage"
---

<div class="lab-hero">
    <div class="hero-content">
        <div class="disclaimer" style="background-color: #fff3cd; border: 2px solid #ffc107; padding: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; border-radius: 0.5rem;">
            <strong>⚠️ Work in Progress:</strong> This interactive lab is currently under development. Some features may be incomplete or unavailable. Content and functionality are subject to change.
        </div>
        <h1 class="hero-title">The Great Exchange</h1>
        <p class="hero-subtitle">Interactive Economic History Lab</p>
        <p class="hero-description">
            Experience the emergence of money through character-driven storytelling, 
            agent-based simulations, and progressive learning activities set in 
            ancient Mesopotamia circa 3500 BCE.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <a href="/great-exchange/chapters/01-the-problem/" class="button large primary">
                Start the Journey
            </a>
            <a href="/great-exchange/simulations/" class="button large secondary">
                Jump to Simulations
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="lab-overview">
    <div class="grid-container">
        <div class="grid-x grid-margin-x">
            <div class="cell large-4">
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <div class="feature-icon">📚</div>
                    <h3>Narrative Learning</h3>
                    <p>
                        Follow Kael, Tira, and Jorek as they navigate the challenges 
                        of ancient trade and discover how money emerges from individual 
                        decisions and social learning.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cell large-4">
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <div class="feature-icon">🎮</div>
                    <h3>Interactive Simulations</h3>
                    <p>
                        Run agent-based simulations based on the Kiyotaki-Wright model 
                        to see how storage costs and search frictions lead to the 
                        emergence of commodity money.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cell large-4">
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <div class="feature-icon">📊</div>
                    <h3>Real-Time Analytics</h3>
                    <p>
                        Watch as trading efficiency improves by 40-60% when over 80% 
                        of trades begin using the low-storage-cost commodity as money.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="lab-characters">
    <div class="grid-container">
        <h2>Meet the Characters</h2>
        <div class="grid-x grid-margin-x">
            {% for character in civilization.characters %}
            <div class="cell large-4">
                <div class="character-card">
                    <div class="character-avatar">{{ character.name | first }}</div>
                    <h4>{{ character.name }}</h4>
                    <p class="character-title">{{ character.title }}</p>
                    <p class="character-description">{{ character.description }}</p>
                    <div class="character-details">
                        <div class="detail">
                            <strong>Produces:</strong> {{ character.production | join(", ") }}
                        </div>
                        <div class="detail">
                            <strong>Needs:</strong> {{ character.consumption | join(", ") }}
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="lab-learning-path">
    <div class="grid-container">
        <h2>Learning Path</h2>
        <div class="learning-steps">
            <div class="step">
                <div class="step-number">1</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                    <h4>The Problem</h4>
                    <p>Discover the double coincidence of wants problem through failed trades at the Festival of Failed Trades.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <div class="step-number">2</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                    <h4>First Exchange</h4>
                    <p>Experience basic bilateral matching and understand why direct exchange often fails.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <div class="step-number">3</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                    <h4>Storage Costs</h4>
                    <p>Learn how different commodities have different storage costs that affect trading decisions.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <div class="step-number">4</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                    <h4>Speculation</h4>
                    <p>See how agents begin accepting goods they don't personally consume to facilitate future trades.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <div class="step-number">5</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                    <h4>Emergence</h4>
                    <p>Witness the emergence of money as one commodity becomes the preferred medium of exchange.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <div class="step-number">6</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                    <h4>Modern Connections</h4>
                    <p>Connect ancient monetary emergence to contemporary economic phenomena and digital currencies.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="lab-simulations">
    <div class="grid-container">
        <h2>Interactive Simulations</h2>
        <div class="grid-x grid-margin-x">
            {% for level in scenarios.simulationLevels %}
            <div class="cell large-6">
                <div class="simulation-card">
                    <h4>{{ level.name }}</h4>
                    <p class="simulation-description">{{ level.description }}</p>
                    <div class="simulation-meta">
                        <span class="complexity">Complexity: {{ level.complexity }}/4</span>
                        <span class="agents">{{ level.agents }} Agent Types</span>
                        <span class="commodities">{{ level.commodities }} Commodities</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="simulation-objectives">
                        <h6>Learning Objectives:</h6>
                        <ul>
                            {% for objective in level.learningObjectives %}
                            <li>{{ objective }}</li>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <a href="/great-exchange/simulations/{{ level.id }}/" class="button">
                        Try Simulation
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
